<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad I al-Mustansir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1228–1277</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad I al-Mustansir was the Hafsid ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a> from 1249 to 1277 and the first of the dynasty to take the title of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>, in 1253. His prestige grew after the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a> and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>, and in 1270 he withstood the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eighth-crusade">Eighth Crusade</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-of-france">Louis IX of France</a>, who died before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a>. His death was followed by succession struggles.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muhammad-i-al-mustansir.jpg" alt="Muhammad I al-Mustansir" width="320" height="169" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DrFO.Jr.Tn · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hafsid_dinar_-_Tunisia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
